  "notes": "Source: official WCU Department of Mathematics & Computer Science eight-semester plan PDF (\"Eight Semester Plan: Computer Science, B.S. Degree\", dated October 2025), still posted as the current department sequence at https://www.wcu.edu/learn/departments-schools-colleges/cas/science-and-math/mathcsdept/bs-computer-science/resources/CS_EightSemesterPlanC1.pdf (retrieved 2026-09-30). WCU online catalog program page: https://catalog.wcu.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=41&poid=5591 (links to this same 8-semester guide). Transcription method: row-by-row transcription of the official PDF tables into per-term slot lists; course titles, credits, and prereqs cross-checked against WCU catalog course descriptions (catalog.wcu.edu). Caveats: (1) The department publishes two track variants; this file encodes the CALCULUS I SEQUENCE variant (student starts in MATH 153). A PRECALCULUS SEQUENCE variant exists (starts MATH 146) but is not encoded. (2) The plan states 'Initial math course should be determined by placement' — students placing below Calculus I follow the precalculus variant. (3) MATH 270-or-370 statistics requirement encoded as a student-choice slot with both options. (4) 'Science' 4-credit slots encoded as choice slots; the major's approved natural-science list is BIOL 140/141, CHEM 139/140, GEOL 150/155, PHYS 130/131 or 230/231 (from the catalog program page). (5) Liberal Studies / General Elective / CS Elective rows encoded as student-choice slots with descriptive titles; no specific courses invented. (6) The department note about the Upper Level Perspective (ULP) Liberal Studies requirement is preserved in a choice_note. (7) CS 495 requires 70 completed credit hours and C or better in CS 253 and CS 351; grade-of-C thresholds from the catalog program page are documented in prereqs as simple course codes (the plan app must read this note for the grade detail). catalog_year is the academic year of the October 2025 dated sequence PDF.",
